{}," is merged per slot",": with a site-wide ",[258,1481,1482],{},"radioGroup.ui.fieldset"," and a page passing ",[258,1485,1486],{},":ui=\"{ item: '...' }\"",", both apply. If the page also passes ",[258,1489,1490],{},"fieldset",", the page value replaces the site-wide one (classes are not concatenated). The result is then merged with the component's built-in styles using tailwind-merge, as in ",[283,1493,1495,1496,1498],{"href":1494},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Ftheming#per-component-ui-prop","Per-component ",[258,1497,1269],{}," prop",". The title bar parts of ",[258,1501,1502],{},"queryCard.ui",[258,1504,1505],{},"listCard.ui",[258,1507,1508],{},"bar",[258,1510,1345],{},[258,1512,1513],{},"title",[258,1515,1516],{},"headerRight",") share the same built-in styles; to make both cards' titles match, set the same values on both.",[1452,1519,1520,1523,1524,1526],{},[973,1521,1522],{},"Other values are replaced as a whole",": arrays (such as ",[258,1525,1330],{},") are not concatenated with the built-in value.",[1452,1528,1529,1532,1533,1535,1536,1538,1539,1542,1543,1546,1547,287],{},[258,1530,1531],{},"inputNumber.unit"," site-wide only decides whether a unit is shown by default and only accepts ",[258,1534,1099],{}," \u002F ",[258,1537,1062],{},"; the unit text comes from ",[258,1540,1541],{},"messages.inputNumber.unit",". A single field can still pass ",[258,1544,1545],{},"unit=\"pcs\""," or ",[258,1548,1549],{},":unit=\"false\"",[1452,1551,1552,1553,1535,1555,1557,1558,1561,1562,1565,1566,1569,1570,987],{},"After setting ",[258,1554,1208],{},[258,1556,1214],{}," site-wide to ",[258,1559,1560],{},"{ Code, Name }",", if a page's items are still ",[258,1563,1564],{},"{ label, value }",", pass ",[258,1567,1568],{},"label-key=\"label\" value-key=\"value\""," on that component. Radio and checkbox groups still bind string values, so convert numeric codes from the back end to strings first. In development mode, when items are missing a field, the console warning